<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	The Mac Catalyst build only — project.yml attaches this with an
	[sdk=macosx*] condition, because neither key means anything on iOS, where
	the app is sandboxed unconditionally and may open outgoing connections
	without asking.

	Both keys are load-bearing on the Mac. A Catalyst app must adopt the App
	Sandbox, and a sandboxed app with no network-client entitlement cannot open
	an outgoing connection at all — so the app would launch, look entirely
	healthy, and fail every request to the user's server with what appears to
	be an unreachable-host error. That is the failure this file prevents, and
	it is not one the iOS build can ever reproduce.

	The keychain access group is the third, and it is not optional either.
	`Keychain` asks for the **data protection** keychain rather than the old
	file-based macOS one, so that a password is the same item under both builds
	and `kSecAttrAccessible` actually means something. A sandboxed Mac app may
	use the file-based keychain freely, but the data protection keychain needs
	the app to be signed into an access group — without one every write fails
	with `errSecMissingEntitlement` and every read afterwards finds nothing.
	Nothing reports that at the time; it surfaces later as a saved server whose
	password has vanished, which reads as a bug in the editor.

	`$(AppIdentifierPrefix)$(CFBundleIdentifier)` is the group every app
	implicitly has. Declaring it explicitly asks for nothing new — it is not
	the Keychain Sharing capability — it just makes the implicit group reachable
	from the data protection keychain.

	Nothing else is granted. Reading files the user picks, and the incoming
	connections a future Cast bridge might want, are separate entitlements to
	be added when the phase that needs them arrives.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)$(CFBundleIdentifier)</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
